# Exhaustive per-row tests for iso-kat-Geor-Latn-9984-2026, generated from the source
# document's table.
# Source: ISO 9984:2026(en), second edition, purchased published edition
# (ISO Store order OP-1130631, downloaded 2026-11-19; verification-grade
# provenance). Rows in document order: Table 4 rows 1-33 (the 33 characters
# of the current Georgian alphabet; hex column authoritative: ejectives
# carry U+0027 neutral apostrophe, digraphs zh/gh/sh/ch/ts/dz/kh per hex),
# then the §4.2 digraph-disambiguation provision (middle dot U+00B7 inserted
# between the six adjoining source pairs whose romanization would form a
# digraph: გჰ ზჰ სჰ ქჰ თს დზ), then Table 5 rows 1-14 (other characters;
# rows 1-6 unchanged from the 1996 edition). Expected strings are the
# printed Latin column (lowercase; capitalization optional per 4.1.2 and not
# part of the system).
# Provenance artifact: scripts/row-sources/iso-kat-Geor-Latn-9984-2026.json (53 rows).
# generated-by: maps/scripts/gen-row-tests.mjs (2026-11-19); regenerate from the artifact, do not hand-edit.
  "ა" -> "a"
  "ბ" -> "b"
  "გ" -> "g"
  "დ" -> "d"
  "ე" -> "e"
  "ვ" -> "v"
